:\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Are ironic names confusing for small dogs?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Not at all. Your dog has no concept of what Titan or Goliath means in human terms. They simply learn that this particular sound pattern, said in this particular tone, means you are addressing them. The humor and irony are entirely for human enjoyment and do not affect your dog's training or name recognition in any way.\\\"}]]}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"details\\\",\\\"2\\\",{\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"summary\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"What small dog breeds have the most distinctive naming traditions?\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"p\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"Chihuahuas often receive Mexican or Spanish-influenced names (Paco, Frida, Taco). French Bulldogs naturally attract French names (Bijou, Coco, Pascal). Corgis inspire food names (Waffles, Biscuit, Potato) and Welsh names (Bryn, Rhys). Dachshunds — being German — connect to German names and, of course, wiener and sausage puns that are practically mandatory.\\\"}]]}]]}]]}]\\n\"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,\"2f:[\\\"$\\\",\\\"section\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"mt-12\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"h2\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\\\",\\\"children\\\":\\\"🐾 Related Animal Name Generators\\\"}],[\\\"$\\\",\\\"div\\\",null,{\\\"className\\\":\\\"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3\\\",\\\"children\\\":[[\\\"$\\\",\\\"$L3\\\",\\\"rhesus-macaque\\\",{\\\"href\\\":\\\"/animal/rhesus-macaque/\\\",\\\"className\\\":\\\"bg-whi